<ns0:note xmlns:ns0="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:ns1="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" id="fs-id1167836378970">
<ns0:title>Relation</ns0:title>
<ns0:para id="fs-id1167824735594">A <ns0:emphasis effect="bold">relation</ns0:emphasis> is any set of ordered pairs,<ns1:math><ns1:mrow><ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>(</ns1:mo><ns1:mrow><ns1:mi>x</ns1:mi><ns1:mo>,</ns1:mo><ns1:mi>y</ns1:mi></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>)</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow><ns1:mo>.</ns1:mo></ns1:mrow></ns1:math> All the <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">x</ns0:emphasis>-values in the ordered pairs together make up the <ns0:emphasis effect="bold">domain</ns0:emphasis>. All the <ns0:emphasis effect="italics">y</ns0:emphasis>-values in the ordered pairs together make up the <ns0:emphasis effect="bold">range</ns0:emphasis>.</ns0:para>
</ns0:note>
